{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>It is zimah</b>. Onkelos translates (Onkelos on Leviticus 18:17) עֵצַת חֶטְאִין הִיא — it is counsel of sin. And Rashi wrote (Rashi on Leviticus 18:17) that your evil inclination counsels you to sin. But I do not know the reason for this, for in all the forbidden relations, and in all other transgressions, the evil inclination counsels one to sin. Rather, the meaning is that the term זִמָּה was derived from כַּאֲשֶׁר זָמַם לַעֲשׂוֹת לְאָחִיו — as he schemed to do to his brother (Deuteronomy 19:19), and for a fitting thought they call it מְזִמָּה, as in וְלֹא יִבָּצֵר מִמְּךָ מְזִמָּה — and no purpose of yours will be thwarted (Job 42:2), and for lewdness done with scheming thought in secret it is called זִמָּה, in the manner of אִם נִפְתָּה לִבִּי עַל אִשָּׁה — if my heart was enticed toward a woman (Job 31:9), and it is written (Job 31:11) כִּי הִיא זִמָּה וְהוּא עָוֹן פְּלִילִים — for it is zimah, and it is a criminal offense. And likewise וְזִמָּתֵךְ וְתַזְנוּתָיִךְ — and your zimah and your harlotries (Ezekiel 23:29), and זִמַּת זְנוּתֵךְ — the zimah of your harlotry (Jeremiah 13:27) — adultery in secret and in public. In my opinion, Scripture says זִמָּה in the case of a woman and her daughter (here) and a woman and her mother (Leviticus 20:14) in order to condemn the matter, to say that when a man lies with one who is his wife, he will think about the other on account of their closeness and resemblance, and behold, lying with both of them becomes zimah. This is the matter our Rabbis mentioned (Nedarim 20a): וּבָרוֹתִי מִכֶּם הַמֹּרְדִים וְהַפּוֹשְׁעִים בִּי — and I will purge from among you those who rebel and transgress against Me (Ezekiel 20:38) — these are of the nine traits, etc. Therefore Scripture said עֶרְוַת אִשָּׁה וּבִתָּהּ — the nakedness of a woman and her daughter, and likewise it says וְאִישׁ אֲשֶׁר יִקַּח אֶת אִשָּׁה וְאֶת אִמָּהּ זִמָּה הִיא — and a man who takes a woman and her mother, it is zimah (Leviticus 20:14), and it did not say the nakedness of your wife's daughter you shall not uncover, and the nakedness of your wife's mother you shall not uncover. For the reason of Scripture is that from the beginning of the parashah (Leviticus 18:6) it said אִישׁ אִישׁ אֶל כָּל שְׁאֵר בְּשָׂרוֹ לֹא תִקְרְבוּ — a man, a man, to any close flesh you shall not approach, for it prohibited those who are closely related to him on account of being his שְׁאֵר, and it gave regarding them the reason (Leviticus 18:10) כִּי עֶרְוָתְךָ הֵנָּה — for they are your nakedness, and now (Leviticus 18:17–18), when it prohibited the relatives of his wife, it said שַׁאֲרָה הֵנָּה — they are her close flesh, to say that they too are prohibited because they are שְׁאֵר to one another, and lying with both of them would be zimah, as I have explained. And likewise Scripture said (Ezekiel 22:11) וְאִישׁ אֶת כַּלָּתוֹ טִמֵּא בְזִמָּה — and a man defiles his daughter-in-law with zimah, that he defiled her to her husband, for even while she is with him he will think about his father on account of their resemblance. And Scripture called lying with a beast תֶּבֶל הוּא — it is confusion (Leviticus 18:23), because it confuses human seed and animal seed, and likewise it said (Leviticus 20:12) regarding lying with a daughter-in-law תֶּבֶל הוּא — it is confusion, because the father and son intermingle to become like one man to her, to lie with both of them together in thought."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:55:39.714744121Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}